	)
	(text_box "G_LB = LB AND (ACT AND NOT P1D AND RUN_L) AND (HA_ON50 AND HB_OFF150 AND CAPC_N). G_LA = LA AND (ACT AND P1D AND RUN_L) AND (HB_ON50 AND HA_OFF150 AND CAPC_N). CAPC_N (cap not expired) reaches both low-side gates directly as\nwell as through the fault latch and RUN_L, so no single stuck element on the ending path can let a low side run past the cap.\nOrder: G_LB only in phase 1 (ACT, not P1D); G_LA only after phase 1 (P1D). A CMD_LA before phase 1, a second CMD_LB, any command after DONE: ignored. A main controller frozen with its timer toggling gets at most one phase-1\nand one phase-2 pulse per rail cycle, inside the 25 ms cap (R-4).\nHA_ON50: G_HA on >= 41-77 us [CALC] (10 k / 6.8 nF, emptied at once through a BAS116 when G_HA falls). HA_OFF150: G_HA off >= 166-364 us [CALC] (10 k / 27 nF, SN74LVC1G14). Firmware leads are 100 us and 500 us (F-4), above\nboth maxima."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.48 337.116 0)
		(size 254.375 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
