		(uuid "36a97f8f-6fd6-5adb-9e19-6f1d2be56448")
	)
	(text_box "FLT_PRE_N = NOT( RDY AND ( OC_F OR IDLE_F OR SEQ_UV OR CAP_F ) ):\nIDLE_F = IDLE_RAW AND LA_OFF10 AND LB_OFF10 (>= 5 A while neither low side has been enabled for 9 us; R-14).\nSEQ_UV = NOR(BR5_OK, ACT_N, DONE) = rail below 4.5 V during a running sequence.\nCAP_F = NOR(CAPC_N, DONE) = cap expired before the planned end.\nCap: ACT (a latch) charges 249 k / 100 nF C0G +-2 % (emptied only when ACT is cleared by RST_N, through a BAS116); TLV7031 against 0.6345 x BRIDGE_3V3 (57.6 k / 100 k). Expiry 23.7-26.5 ms after the start [CALC] (spec 25 ms\n+-15 % = 21.3-28.8 ms). Non-retriggerable and not extendable: the RC is driven by the ACT latch, which nothing but a power-on reset clears; nothing a controller does can restart or stretch it. CAPC_N is high while not expired;\npower-on reset holds it low = expired.\nFault-path nodes have pull-UPs (a dead gate reads 'fault'); FLT_PRE_N has a pull-DOWN (a dead NAND sets FLT)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 876.385 401.54 0)
		(size 255.62 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "20babdc2-660b-5bc7-ae4b-cfbb61bc3c21")
	)
	(text_box "Patient-relay coil enable K_EN: 90 ms latched coil cap, start window, off 1 ms after the end (§B7.2, §B13.3 rule 7)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 401.51 0)
		(size 243.075 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
