			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b501aa3-0811-5eca-9b0b-17b3802f4609")
	)
	(text_box "K_EN = RELAY_CMD AND NOT TEST_MODE AND KCAP_N AND RUN_D1M AND RDY (KA_N = NAND3, then NOR with TM). RDY is added to rule 7 so that the coil timer's start latch KON can never miss the first K_EN edge while RST_N\nholds it cleared (a RELAY_CMD already high at rail-up would otherwise leave the coil uncapped). In test mode the coil can never be energised: the bridge cannot reach the pads (§B14.2).\nCoil timer: KON (latched at the FIRST K_EN rise) charges 953 k / 100 nF C0G +-2 %; a three-resistor divider (115 k / 66.5 k / 121 k) gives 0.400 and 0.620 x BRIDGE_3V3. KWIN_N (start window) closes 45.7-51.8 ms\nafter the coil was energised; KCAP_N (coil cap) cuts K_EN 87.1-97.6 ms after [CALC]. Latest possible coil-off = 51.8 (latest start) + 26.5 (cap) + 1.63 (coil delay) = 80.0 ms < 87.0 ms: a started sequence always\nends before the coil cap; 97.6 ms < the G17's 100 ms rating (§B7.2). Same RC for both thresholds, so their ratio is set by 0.1 % resistors only.\nBoth comparators are held low by power-on reset = window closed / coil cut (fail to 'no coil').\nOutput to sheet 14 through 1 k (pull-down there)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 407.86 0)
		(size 243.075 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
